## Single row subqueries (Scalar subquery)                                   The subquery functions as a single value (scalar) that the outer query compares against a single value.    

                                                                                                                                                  -- select avg(city_pop) from city;
select * from city
where city_pop >= (select avg(city_pop) from city);


## Multi Row subquries (Table Subquery)                                  An outer query's numerous rows are compared with the multiple rows of data returned by a multi-row subquery.

																													 -- select country_code from country where continent = "Europe";
select ID,city_name,countrycode,city_pop from city
where countrycode in
(select country_code from country
where continent = "Europe");

                                                                      -- Correlated subquery

select * from city C
where exists
(select * from country Co
where continent = "Europe"
And c.countrycode = co.country_code);

